  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall be begun before the expiration of three years from the date of this permission.",
    "Condition : 2 - The proposed development shall be carried out in all respects in accordance with the proposals contained in the application and the plans submitted (18903 - P001, 18903 - P002, 18903 - P005, 18903 - P006, 18903 - P006 Rev A, 18903 - P007, 18903 - P110, SL07099-HBPW-00-ZZ-DR-C-0100 Rev P1, Cover Letter (ref. CF/P21-0121) prepared by Pegasus Group, [dated 11 March 2021], Acoustic Assessment (ref. 210305-R001), prepared by ACA Acoustics [dated 16 March 2021], received on 25/03/2021; 18903 - P103 Rev B & 18903 - P110 Rev B, received on 16/04/2021; 18903 - P105, received on 14/05/2021) therewith and approved by the Local Planning Authority, or as shall have been otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority before the building is used.",
    "Condition : 3 - The cycle parking arrangements shall not be carried out otherwise than in accordance with approved plan number 18903 - P103 Rev B for 14 covered Sheffield stands providing 28 cycle parking spaces and shall be implemented before the use hereby approved is commenced and shall thereafter be retained as such.",
    "Condition : 4 - The levels of disabled persons parking for Blue Badge holders shall not be carried out otherwise than in accordance with approved plan number 18903 - P103 Rev B for at least 4 Blue Badge bays and shall be implemented before the use hereby approved is commenced and shall thereafter be retained as such for the lifetime of the development.",
    "Condition : 5 - The building at Spitfire Logistics Centre, Spitfire Way shall not be used for purposes other than those within Class B2 (industrial), Class E(g)(iii) (industrial processes) and/or Class B8 (storage and distribution) and for no other purpose (including any other purpose within the Schedule to the Town and Country Planning (Use Classes) Order 1987, or in any provision equivalent to that Class in any statutory instrument revoking and re-enacting that Order with or without modification)."
  ],
